From 5fb9b490c26ca8676a4b2daa1990e97e62c813f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jimmy <fakeandroit@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:43:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] clk: samsung: exynos7870: add Exynos7880 CMU_CCORE

Exynos7880 has no CMU_MIF; its CMU_CCORE holds BUS_PLL and MEDIA_PLL and
generates the clocks for the other CMUs. Those outputs (muxes 0x264-0x2cc,
dividers 0x460-0x4cc, gates 0x860-0x8cc) and the BUSD, APB and HSI2C
dividers use the same offsets and bit fields as the Exynos7870 CMU_MIF;
the PLL and BUSD muxes, the HSI2C and ADC_IF gates differ, and there is
no MEM_PLL. Register offsets and fields were checked one by one against
the vendor kernel's S5E7880-cmusfr.h and S5E7880-cmu.c.

Keep the CMU_MIF clock names and IDs, so the CMU_FSYS, CMU_G3D and
CMU_PERI drivers, which find their parents by those names, are shared
with Exynos7870 unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
